# 🚑 TRAFFICORE Setup Guide

## Overview
This guide will help you set up the complete TRAFFICORE system with:
- ✅ Real-time patient data via MQTT
- ✅ GPS tracking of ambulance
- ✅ Doctor-Ambulance chat system
- ✅ Live camera stream

---

## 📋 Prerequisites

### Raspberry Pi (Ambulance Side)
- Raspberry Pi 4 or 3B+
- Raspbian OS installed
- Python 3.7+
- Camera module (optional)
- GPS module (optional, can simulate)

### Hospital Dashboard (Computer/Server)
- Modern web browser (Chrome, Firefox, Edge)
- Web server (Apache, Nginx, or Python's HTTP server)

---

## 🔧 Part 1: Raspberry Pi Setup

### 1. Install Mosquitto MQTT Broker

```bash
# Update system
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install Mosquitto broker and clients
sudo apt install mosquitto mosquitto-clients -y

# Enable Mosquitto to start on boot
sudo systemctl enable mosquitto
```

### 2. Configure Mosquitto

```bash
# Create configuration file
sudo nano /etc/mosquitto/conf.d/mosquitto.conf
```

Copy the content from the **Mosquitto Configuration** artifact, then:

```bash
# Restart Mosquitto
sudo systemctl restart mosquitto

# Check status
sudo systemctl status mosquitto
```

### 3. Install Python MQTT Library

```bash
# Install paho-mqtt
pip3 install paho-mqtt

# Or if you get permission errors
pip3 install --user paho-mqtt
```

### 4. Set Up the Ambulance Script

```bash
# Create a directory for the project
mkdir ~/trafficore
cd ~/trafficore

# Create the Python script
nano ambulance_sender.py
```

Copy the content from the **Raspberry Pi MQTT Sender** artifact, then:

```bash
# Make it executable
chmod +x ambulance_sender.py

# Run it
python3 ambulance_sender.py
```

### 5. Find Your Pi's IP Address

```bash
hostname -I
```

Note this IP address - you'll need it for the dashboard!

